    "body": "@anforowicz I could see https://github.com/annevk/orb having an early step to check _mimeType_'s essence for one of those types (edit: in my mind, the more types the merrier) and then return false, which would then result in a network error. I would be supportive of adding that behavior to the specification. It would be similar to [the existing MIME type blocking](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#should-response-to-request-be-blocked-due-to-mime-type?) but for opaque responses only.",
